# Taking from the world, as it is SEEN (owner 2026-09-17): what the use key would
# work is marked where it stands, what is taken is said on the HUD with its own
# mark, and a thing taken in goes stands smaller with each until the last go takes
# it away. Everything is found by name, never by a coordinate.
#
#   tools/tour.sh tours/harvest.tour --seed=1 --hour=11 --weather=clear:0 --give=pick:1 --held=pick
#
# The mark is the interim drawing (src/ui/ui_harvest_mark.gd says why); the rule
# under it is Harvest.target, the same choice the key makes.
coast calm
zoom 9
# A stone seam with a pick in hand: marked as workable.
near stone_ore
wait 0.6
shot 01-a-seam-the-pick-would-work with harvest_target:workable,prop:stone_ore
# One go: stone in the creel, said with its mark, and a third of the seam off it.
press use 0.1
await picked_up:stone 20
wait 0.4
shot 02-one-go-a-third-off-it with worked_down,prop:stone_ore
# A second go on the same seam: two stone more, merged into the same row.
press use 0.1
await took 20
wait 0.4
shot 03-two-goes-a-stump-of-a-seam with worked_down,prop:stone_ore
# The last go takes it away.
press use 0.1
await took 20
wait 1.2
shot 04-the-seam-worked-out
# A copper seam: the iron pick rings off it, and the mark says so before the key does.
near copper_ore
wait 0.6
shot 05-copper-too-hard-for-iron with harvest_target:too_hard,prop:copper_ore
# A bush picked bare stands whole, marked only by the ring.
near bush
press use 0.1
await took 12
wait 0.6
shot 06-a-bush-picked-over with harvest_target:picked_over,prop:bush
